--- Expression with rand ---

-- Define a hero
There is a "Hero Name" of kind string that should listen to me.
There is a "Hero Health" of kind number that is _100_.

-- The adventure begins
This is a tale "Battle with the Dragon".
So it begins.
    Say `A fearsome dragon appears before ` and the meaning of "Hero Name".

    -- Roll a dice (simulate randomness)
    There is a "Dice Roll" of kind number that is _randint(1, 6)_.

    If the meaning of "Dice Roll" is greater than 3,
    Then
        Say `With a mighty swing, ` and the meaning of "Hero Name" and ` defeats the dragon!`.
        Then "Hero Health" became _$"Hero Health" + 20_.
    Otherwise,
        Say `The dragon breathes fire! ` and the meaning of "Hero Name" and ` takes damage.`.
        Then "Hero Health" became the meaning of "Hero Health" - 30.
    The end.

    Say `Hero's health: ` and the meaning of "Hero Health".
The end.

-- Start the adventure
Tell me a tale "Battle with the Dragon".
